From 3a4848a30b5b6e1dfb2a8202c09f5e2754cf7f6d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mohammed <91819504+mohammed7s@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 00:11:04 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] computercontrol: let the user manage the user allowlist

Add four methods to IComputerControlConsentManager to read and change the
user allowlist added in the previous change:

  isPackageApprovedToRunAutomationByUser / setPackageApprovedToRunAutomationByUser
  isPackageTargetableForAutomationByUser / setPackageTargetableForAutomationByUser

Like the existing per-agent consent methods they require
MANAGE_COMPUTER_CONTROL_CONSENT, which is signature-level and held by
Settings and the consent dialog. Acting on another user also requires
INTERACT_ACROSS_USERS_FULL. They do nothing while computer_control_access
is off.

Withdrawing an agent closes its ongoing sessions; withdrawing a target
closes any session automating it, as removing a per-agent consent entry
already does.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
